("`AbortSignal.timeout` and `AbortSignal.any` are more recent than `AbortController` itself; ⚠ *verify support against your browser matrix.* A distinction","`AbortSignal.timeout` and `AbortSignal.any` are more recent than `AbortController` itself (versions above); check them against your browser matrix. Verified in Node 24 by running `fetch` against a local server: a default `abort()` rejects with a `DOMException` named `AbortError` (identical to `signal.reason`), `abort(new Error('x'))` rejects with that custom reason, `AbortSignal.timeout(20)` rejects with a `DOMException` named `TimeoutError`, `AbortSignal.any` propagates the first source's reason, and a body read after `abort()` also rejects with `AbortError`. A distinction"),
